723d94cc899f3ad2c75fbf49f9192984  post_badge8.ss1  PINNED  THE §Ch22 OUTPUT FIXTURE — and §Ch23's START. Captured 2026-09-03 by `--driver ch22chapter` with `CH22_CAPTURE` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (badge, out of the gym, b1f_entered, battles_on_B1F=0, CONTINUE=23), so the file's EXISTENCE is the acceptance record. Probe-verified (probe_anchor_inventory, whose own positive control passed first): OVERWORLD SOOTOPOLIS_CITY (31,33), **badges=12345678 — ALL EIGHT**, party 6. ⚠⚠ **428/701 (61%) WITH ONE MEMBER FAINTED** — the probe itself flags it "CANNOT SURVIVE A JOURNEY". This is NOT a defect in the fixture: §Ch22 genuinely chews the party (contrast `post_hm07.ss1` at 91% with none down), because the Juan fight is stochastic and the chapter may fight it twice. ⇒ **§Ch23's FIRST act must be a heal**, and its preflight must assert the party by PID afterwards — the Sootopolis Poke Center is 23 wp away and measured reachable. ⛔ AND THE OCEAN LEG THAT FOLLOWS HAS NO ESCAPE: `allow_escaping: false` on Sootopolis, Routes 126/127/128 and every underwater map, with NO Poke Center until Ever Grande. ‼ Wailmer is the SOLE Dive carrier and Dive is the ONLY exit from the crater — any change that could cost it strands the run. (As of this capture Wailmer knows Dive/Surf/Water Gun/Rollout; `--driver ch23teach` replaces Rollout with Waterfall and KEEPS both HMs.)
3eec11dbaa5deae51288cfa34e198536  post_waterfall.ss1  PINNED  §Ch23's WORKING START — `post_badge8.ss1` with WATERFALL TAUGHT. Captured 2026-09-03 by `--driver ch23teach` with `CH23_CAPTURE` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (Waterfall present by PID, Dive AND Surf both survived, party intact 6->6), so the file's EXISTENCE is the record. Driver-verified: Wailmer#FA51ECF3 = Dive / Surf / Water Gun / **Waterfall** (Rollout was the move forgotten — slot 3, the deepest forget-menu scroll this bot has driven). Probe-verified (`--driver ch23route`, read-only): all EIGHT badges, SOOTOPOLIS_CITY (31,33), **ROUTE128_STATE=2** (the ON_FRAME Kyogre scene is SPENT), and the bag holds HM02/03/04/06/07/08 but **NOT HM01 Cut and NOT HM05 Flash**. ⛔⛔ **WAILMER IS THE SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE FOR THE WHOLE CHAPTER** — it is the SOLE carrier of Dive (the only exit from the Sootopolis crater) AND of Waterfall (the only way up to Victory Road), and it also carries Surf. Anything that could deposit or lose it strands the run; §Ch23's preflight must assert it BY PID. ⛔⛔ **THE FAINTED MEMBER IS WAILMER ITSELF — measured 2026-09-03 by `--driver partypids`: `Wailmer#FA51ECF3 hp=0/160 FAINTED`, Swellow 5/118 (4%), the other four at 100%.** So the chapter's SOLE Dive+Waterfall carrier starts DEAD, and the opening heal is a HARD PRECONDITION, not hygiene. ‼ This entry previously said only "61% HP with one member fainted" while naming the SPOF in a separate sentence; the hazard is their CONJUNCTION and nothing joined them. ⇒ assert Wailmer ALIVE **by PID** — a party count reads 6 either way.
5e1652cbea9449fd7d6073a53c28e865  post_depart_sootopolis.ss1  PINNED  **THE §Ch23 LEGS 2-3 OUTPUT FIXTURE — the first fixture this project has ever had OUTSIDE the Sootopolis crater on the Ever Grande arc.** Captured 2026-09-03 by `--driver ch23depart` with `CH23_CAPTURE` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (all 10 readings, `missing=[]`, trace in order, `crater_exits=1`, `whiteouts=0`, `attempts_used=1`), so the file's EXISTENCE is the acceptance record. Probe-verified (`probe_anchor_inventory`): OVERWORLD **ROUTE126 (45,66)**, badges=12345678, party 6 at **701/701 (100%)**. ⭐⭐ **THIS IS A STRICTLY BETTER START THAN `post_waterfall.ss1`** — that one is 428/701 (61%) with **Wailmer FAINTED**; legs 2-3 heal it, so leg 4 begins on a full party with the sole Dive/Waterfall carrier alive. ⭐ Driver-verified on the way through: the dive tile reads `'Sootopolis Deep Water'`, the underwater arrival is **(9,6)** exactly as predicted, the arrow warp rests on **(45,66)** (NOT its target (45,65) — the 'step south' branch never executes), the emerge tile type is **`'Normal'`** (the first time this tree has ever read it), and `calculate_path` off the end tile is **55 wp** to the Route 126 east edge, matching `ch23route` R9f exactly. ⛔ The whiteout respawn was ALREADY armed to Sootopolis `(0,7)` on entry (§Ch22 had entered that Center), so the re-arm branch did NOT execute on this capture — it is built and gated but **UNPROVEN**; the `STALERESPAWN` arm is still owed. ⚠ And the layout pin was a **NO-OP here** (`0x083E6A04 -> 0x083E6A04`) because §Ch21 never ran in this process to leave a stale pin. Its protective value is real but is **not demonstrated by this capture** — it only bites in a full `_play()` run.
18203e997edcc6326b6d143f7764c237  post_ever_grande.ss1  PINNED  **THE §Ch23 LEG-4 OUTPUT FIXTURE — THE FIRST STATE THIS PROJECT HAS EVER HAD *ABOVE* THE EVER GRANDE WATERFALL, i.e. on Victory Road's doorstep.** Captured 2026-09-04 by `--driver ch23cross` with `CH23_CAPTURE` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (all 9 readings, `missing=[]`, trace in order, `whiteouts=0`), so the file's EXISTENCE is the acceptance record. Probe-verified (`probe_anchor_inventory`): OVERWORLD **EVER_GRANDE_CITY (18,42)**, badges=12345678, party 6 at **701/701 (100%)**. ⭐⭐ **THE RESPAWN IS ARMED TO EVER_GRANDE `(0,8)`, NOT SOOTOPOLIS** — leg 4 walks into the Ever Grande Poké Center for exactly this reason. Until that happens a whiteout inside Victory Road lands **below the falls, back inside the crater**, forcing a re-run of legs 3 AND 4. ⛔ **(18,42) IS THE APRON, NOT THE DOOR.** (18,41) is the Victory Road **warp**, and `calculate_path` to it returns a plan whose last waypoint is `VICTORY_ROAD_1F (15,40) is_warp=True` (MEASURED, `ch23route` R11b) — aiming there would have ended leg 4 *inside the cave*, silently doing leg 5's job. ⭐ Driver-verified en route: `maps_seen` = {ROUTE126, ROUTE127, ROUTE128, EVER_GRANDE} (the PRESENCE witness — a run that never left ROUTE126 fails), lead put in slot 0 = **Sceptile#863B0917**, waterfall base tile `'Ocean Water'`, climb ended **(18,59)** exactly as predicted, and `calculate_path` off the end tile = **22 wp** to the Poké Center apron. ⚠ Leg 5 starts HERE and its first act is `_walk_through_warp` NORTH onto (18,41).
2f517f1f790b0151af9a7837ac493e4e  post_training.ss1  PINNED  **THE §Ch23 TRAINING OUTPUT FIXTURE — THE FIRST STATE THIS PROJECT HAS EVER HAD THAT IS *READY FOR WALLY*.** ⛔⛔ **IT IS *NOT* READY FOR THE ELITE FOUR, AND THIS ROW SAID SO FOR ONE COMMIT — CORRECTED 2026-09-04 AFTER THE EVIDENCE CONTRADICTED IT.** This party beat Wally (ace **L45**) at the cost of **two faints and 67% HP**; the Elite Four run **L46-58** and Wallace's team is **L55-58** with four Full Restores and a Recover/Sitrus Milotic. L47 was chosen because it is the highest target AFFORDABLE on 1F and Mightyena's Crunch level — never because it clears the League. ⇒ the remaining gap is meant to be closed on **B1F after Wally**. ‼ *An overclaim in a fixture row is the most expensive kind: it is what a future session reads to decide the party is ready.* Captured 2026-09-04 by `--driver ch23train` with `CH23_CAPTURE` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (`ACCEPTANCE: PASS`, **battles=132, whiteouts=0**), so the file's EXISTENCE is the acceptance record. Probe-verified (`probe_anchor_inventory --filter post_training`): OVERWORLD **VICTORY_ROAD_1F (15,39)**, badges=12345678, party 6 — **Sceptile L51, Zigzagoon L19, Swellow L47, Wailord L47, Mightyena L47, Castform L36**, HP 754/796 (95%). ⭐⭐ **MIGHTYENA KNOWS CRUNCH** — the run log carries the literal `MIGHTYENA learned CRUNCH!`, and that is the binding constraint of the whole arc: Emerald has NO Dark TM, so a Mightyena that reached 47 without the level-up learn could never answer Phoebe's Ghosts. ⭐ **Wailmer EVOLVED INTO WAILORD at L41** en route, and the identity tracking survived it (PID `FA51ECF3` unchanged) — which is exactly why this leg asserts on PID and never on species or slot. ⛔ **THIS FIXTURE ONLY EXISTS BECAUSE OF KI-84.** The first attempt at the same grind, from the same start, produced **8 battles** and stalled at Wailmer L41 / Swellow L42, because `train_team(slots={i})` with `i != 0` runs ONE spin-batch and returns as if finished (it re-reads `party[i]` by index after SWAPPING that mon to slot 0). The leg now rotates to slot 0 first and calls `train_team(slots={0})`. ⚠ **(15,39) IS AN ENCOUNTER TILE** — `'Cave'`, one step from the 1F entrance warp — so a run resuming here can meet a wild Pokémon on its first step; that is intended (it is the training spot), not a defect. ⚠ Zigzagoon L19 and Castform L36 are DELIBERATELY untrained bench (typing, not levels, is their problem) — they are still in the party and a faint cascade can send them in. ⚠ HP is 95%, not 100%: heal before Wally.
